--- (5) VERDICT: item 9 VERIFIED; reviewer finding F10 REPRODUCED ---
All three acceptance clauses are asserted, by value, with "no run created" proved
four ways (h.invokes==[], runRows()==[], no epic/ticket Lambda call, 200-not-4xx).
The tombstone carries deleted:true and IS excluded by dynamo-read.ts:36
(`items.filter(item => item.deleted !== true)`) and :53 (getWorkflow -> null).

F10 REPRODUCED. evaluateSweepCadence counts ANY prior sweep row for the def+repo.
The filter at :163-170 tests four things -- deleted!==true, type!=='skipped',
workflowDefId and repo key -- and NEVER phase. So a sweep that ERRORED or was
CANCELLED one day ago suppresses the next 14 days of scheduled ticks exactly as a
clean delivery would. The doc comment at :125-128 enumerates the inclusions it
means to make ("including one still running... including one that closed
nothing-to-remove") and the exclusions ("Deliberately NOT counted: ... tombstones
... deleted rows") -- error/cancelled appear in neither list, so this reads as an
oversight rather than a decision.

COVERAGE GAP: sweep-cadence.test.ts covers phase 'complete', 'development'
(running) and 'nothing-to-remove'. No test uses 'error' or 'cancelled' as a real
prior run, so nothing pins today's behaviour either way.

SEVERITY: low-moderate and self-limiting. A crashed sweep blocks only SCHEDULED
starts; "Run now" (trigger !== 'scheduled') is ungated (:12-13, and the test
"does not gate a MANUAL run of the same routine, even with a 3-day-old sweep").
Under the shipped shadow default nothing is skipped at all.

